/**
 * Files a program needs, named by a string literal where the signature says what kind of file it is
 * (docs/design/RESOURCES.md): a [Resource] ships beside the program and is read while it runs, an [EmbeddedBytes] and
 * an [EmbeddedText] are in the binary. A literal where one of them is expected is resolved by the compiler against the
 * file that writes it, and a file that is not there is an error at that line; a `String` value never becomes one.
 *
 *     fn load(sheet: Resource): String {
 *       sheet.name()
 *     }
 *
 *     print load("./hero.png")
 *
 * This is slice 1 of the design: the types, the literal and the stable name. Reading the bytes - embedding them and
 * shipping them - is slices 2 and 3.
 */

public use Resource, EmbeddedBytes, EmbeddedText from "./resource"
